WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:07.620
All of these personal experiences don't
involve you speaking, don't involve you

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.500
in any way having to be an extrovert.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.180
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here again
to talk about language learning.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.740
And today I want to talk about
language learning and the introvert

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.660
or people who are introverted.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.080
Remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:28.275
Uh, if you follow me
on a podcast service...

00:00:28.305 --> 00:00:30.765
oh yes, and by the way, click
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:30.765 --> 00:00:35.025
If you follow me on a podcast
service, please leave a review.

00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:41.505
So my last or one of my most
recent interviews was a discussion

00:00:41.505 --> 00:00:43.455
with Gabriel from Brazil.

00:00:44.055 --> 00:00:49.395
I have spoken to other people about
language learning in different languages.

00:00:49.455 --> 00:00:56.655
And I would think that many of the people
who show up on YouTube as polyglots or

00:00:56.685 --> 00:01:02.565
talk about language learning, including
myself, are probably extroverts.

00:01:02.655 --> 00:01:04.035
In other words, I'm not shy.

00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:09.705
If I go to a party and I see people I
want to talk and interact with people

00:01:09.705 --> 00:01:16.230
and I'm not shy sbout sharing my views
on different subjects and so forth.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.460
So I am an extrovert.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.140
I think Gabriel is an extrovert.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:24.060
Someone commented that, you
know, it seems, saying to me, you

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.240
always have extroverts on there
talking about language learning.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.229
What about introverts who
want to learn languages?

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:33.570
So I thought I would
talk a bit about that.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.030
I don't think being an extrovert
is a condition for being

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.000
a polyglot or a linguist.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:46.350
Remember that if you look up the word
"linguist" in an English language

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:50.580
dictionary, the first meaning is
someone who speaks several languages.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.130
The second meaning one that has developed
much later in history is this idea

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.410
of someone who studies linguistics.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:04.630
The word "polyglot" just means
many tongues or many languages.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:11.280
So, if you are a person who is interested
in languages, because you like to

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.140
read in different languages, which
is my case, and you like to discover

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.960
different languages and you enjoy this
very personal experience of let's say,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.870
reading in different languages or even
listening in different languages on

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.370
subjects of interest to you, listening
to voices that you're like enjoying

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.660
the sound of different language....

00:02:34.455 --> 00:02:40.725
all of these personal experiences
don't involve you speaking, don't

00:02:40.725 --> 00:02:49.215
involve you in any way having to be
an extrovert, being outgoing and "hail

00:02:49.215 --> 00:02:51.825
fellow well met" or any of these things.

00:02:53.175 --> 00:03:01.584
So you can be a wonderful polyglot,
linguist language learner and decide

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.960
to totally focus on input only.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:09.100
Now I think the majority of
people who focus on input

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.380
at some stage want to speak.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.690
It's normal for people to want to speak,
but even the desire to speak doesn't

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:20.590
mean that you're always looking for an
opportunity to speak, that you're sort

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:25.780
of naturally bursting to say things
which is sort of the, uh, characteristics

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:27.970
that we associate with an extrovert.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.739
You can be somewhat introverted.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.110
That doesn't mean you're not a deep
thinker, but you don't necessarily

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:37.440
want to share those thoughts
with other people all the time.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.140
That's more in, it's sort of
along the lines of an introvert.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.220
You don't have to speak to demonstrate
that you are learning the language.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:48.030
You don't have to demonstrate your
prowess or your, your level of

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:52.640
fluency in speaking in order to
qualify as a polyglot in my mind.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.560
Now, if you want to say I speak a language
fluently, then you have to demonstrate

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.370
that you speak that language fluently
if you're claiming to speak it fluently.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.390
And remember, I feel you can be
fluent and still make mistakes, but

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:10.320
at least you can express your opinions
comfortably in a way that makes

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.300
the other person feel comfortable.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.730
But a big part, obviously, of
being fluent is that you understand

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.620
what the other person is saying.

00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:24.390
So even there, it does start with
this basically inward oriented

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.360
process of learning languages,
but you don't have to speak.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:32.910
And I've mentioned before, uh, maybe 50
years ago, I was in Europe, in a, in a bar

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:37.590
somewhere and there was, uh, a person, a
student from Japan who could communicate

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.410
in 13 languages, but he was deaf mute.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.840
I don't know what the politically
correct term is today, but

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.140
he couldn't make sounds.

00:04:44.535 --> 00:04:48.825
But we would write questions to him
in 13 languages and he would answer

00:04:48.885 --> 00:04:51.255
those questions in those 13 languages.

00:04:51.465 --> 00:04:56.205
He wasn't an introvert because he, he was
quite comfortable, uh, you know, fielding

00:04:56.205 --> 00:04:57.495
these questions and answering them.

00:04:57.495 --> 00:04:58.604
But he wasn't speaking.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:01.080
So he was communicating and writing.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:06.510
So I just want to make the point that,
uh, and, and it's by no means certain, you

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:10.919
know, I think we've all seen that say in a
class, the person who is sort of bubbling

00:05:10.919 --> 00:05:14.969
and, and, uh, willing to try things
and it's, it's a good thing actually,

00:05:14.969 --> 00:05:17.010
to not be afraid of making mistakes.

00:05:17.429 --> 00:05:20.039
And so that person seems
to speak better earlier.

00:05:21.135 --> 00:05:24.855
Again, that doesn't mean that in the
long run that person will have a better

00:05:24.915 --> 00:05:28.965
understanding of the language, be
able to read better in the language

00:05:29.115 --> 00:05:34.365
than someone who doesn't speak very
much but is more focused on input,

00:05:34.365 --> 00:05:37.615
but more focused on discovering the
language reading in the language.

00:05:37.635 --> 00:05:42.765
So I guess the only part I want to make,
and this is an answer to the question that

00:05:42.765 --> 00:05:47.565
I received, you know, why don't you ever
talk about introverts who learn languages?

00:05:47.595 --> 00:05:54.090
Yes, by all means language learning
is a personal experience activity.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.349
We do it for ourselves.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:01.680
We do it in the way that, that makes us
happy, that satisfies us, that satisfies

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:07.049
our curiosity, our interests, our
personality and whatever degree of...

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.364
and I'm, and because it's not
black and white, people are all

00:06:10.364 --> 00:06:11.984
introverts or all extroverts.

00:06:11.984 --> 00:06:12.945
There's a degree.

00:06:13.094 --> 00:06:17.445
And given certain situations, some
people are more inclined to be bubbling,

00:06:17.445 --> 00:06:19.544
outgoing personalities and others less.

00:06:19.544 --> 00:06:24.614
So wherever you are on the spectrum,
it has nothing to do with a person's

00:06:24.614 --> 00:06:30.375
ability to be a polyglot or a language
learner or a linguist, in my opinion.

00:06:31.065 --> 00:06:35.174
And so I'm going to leave a
couple of video suggestions here.

00:06:35.205 --> 00:06:39.465
If you want to pursue this subject in
some of the videos that I've already made.

00:06:39.795 --> 00:06:40.815
Thank you for listening.

00:06:40.995 --> 00:06:41.355
Bye for now.

